---
import '../../styles/why-now.css';
import OutlineIcon from '../shared/OutlineIcon.astro';
---

<section class="why-now-section section-pad">
  <div class="container split-grid">
    <div class="section-copy">
      <p class="label muted">Why this matters now</p>
      <h2>Class 8–10 is when career confusion quietly becomes career pressure.</h2>
      <p>
        By Class 10, many students are pushed into stream decisions before they fully understand their strengths. The
        earlier parents understand the right decision framework, the easier it becomes to guide the child without
        panic, comparison or pressure.
      </p>
      <div class="why-now-feelings">
        <article>
          <span class="why-now-feelings-icon"><OutlineIcon name="triangle-alert" size={18} /></span>
          <strong>Pressure feels urgent</strong>
          <p>Parents often feel they must decide quickly, even when the family still lacks real clarity.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="why-now-feelings-icon"><OutlineIcon name="shield" size={18} /></span>
          <strong>Clarity reduces damage</strong>
          <p>Earlier understanding helps avoid avoidable stress, spending, and wrong-fit subject commitments.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="why-now-close">
        The right stream decision does not guarantee success. But the wrong stream decision can make the next 3–5
        years unnecessarily difficult.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="why-now-card">
      <h3>Wrong stream choices can lead to:</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><OutlineIcon name="triangle-alert" size={16} /> Loss of motivation</li>
        <li><OutlineIcon name="wallet" size={16} /> Tuition and coaching waste</li>
        <li><OutlineIcon name="heart-handshake" size={16} /> Parent-child conflict</li>
        <li><OutlineIcon name="book-open" size={16} /> Last-minute subject switching</li>
        <li><OutlineIcon name="compass" size={16} /> Confusion after Class 12</li>
        <li><OutlineIcon name="school" size={16} /> Poor fit between degree and career path</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
